**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The pure halves of the slot bar: which kit items a slot's chip lists, which one a typed letter picks, and the angle an object's chip shows (001 §J 'Quick swap: a slot bar above the table shows one chip per slot (… Obj 1: QZ ▾ @ 45° ▾ …); each dropdown lists compatible items only; … keyboard: Tab between chips, letters pick'; the S8.4 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs`, after step 261's members: (1) `PickLetter of char` with `.value`, a letter typed on a chip, and `static member tryCreate (text : string) : PickLetter option`: the first character of the text, upper-cased in the invariant culture, when `Char.IsLetterOrDigit` holds for it, and `None` for an empty text or any other first character. (2) `type SetupSlot with`: (a) `member this.turnAngle : Angle`, the reading of a `DialTurn reading` slot and the placement's R1 otherwise (`PlacementTurn`, or a slot holding nothing): the rule `NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf` applies to an `AnglePlaceholder` (step 271), moved here; that arm in `NamingTemplates.fs` calls it and keeps its condition (Obj k holds an item), so every name it writes is unchanged. (b) `member this.fittingItems (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) : Item list`: the items of `items`, in their order, whose `choiceOf` answers a choice whose `slotKinds` (step 258) holds the slot's `placement.catalogueKind`; an item `choiceOf` cannot resolve is left out. It is the rule `withItem` checks (step 258), applied before the choice, so a chip lists exactly what `SwapSlot` accepts. (c) `member this.pickedByLetter (letter : PickLetter) (fitting : Item list) : Item option`: among `fitting`, the items whose label's first character, upper-cased in the invariant culture, is the letter; when the slot holds one of them (`content.itemOpt`, step 256), the next of them after it, wrapping to the first; otherwise the first of them; and `None` when none is, or when that pick is the item the slot already holds, so a letter never swaps a slot to its own content. No cache, wildcard arm or other member is added. Tests, in `SetupTests` (steps 256-258, 261), over its slots `src`, `lpA`, `sampleA` and `det` (steps 256, 257) and test-local items made as step 258's facts make them, each `FixedMounting` unless named: `Laser` (`SourcePresetChoice` of `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633`), `LP1` and `LP2` (the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` polarizer), `CPL1` (`LibraryModelChoice` of the circular polarizer's built-in item model, `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel`, step 210), `QZ` (`StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1), `QZd` (the glass plate, `DialMounted DialNegative`, its `dialZero` known at 10°) and `Ghost`, which the test-local `choiceOf` answers `None` for. `a slot lists the kit's items that fit it, in their order`: over the items `Laser`, `LP1`, `QZ`, `CPL1`, `Ghost` and `LP2`, in that order, `lpA.fittingItems` is `LP1`, `CPL1`, `LP2`, `sampleA`'s is `QZ`, `src`'s `Laser` and `det`'s none. `a typed letter picks the next fitting item whose label starts with it, wrapping, and never the slot's own`: over `lpA`'s fitting `LP1`, `CPL1`, `LP2`: holding `LP1`, `l` picks `LP2` and `c` picks `CPL1`; holding `LP2`, `L` picks `LP1` (wrapping); holding nothing, `l` picks `LP1`; holding `CPL1`, `c` picks nothing (no other label starts with it); `x` picks nothing; and `PickLetter.tryCreate` of `q` and of `qz` is `PickLetter 'Q'`, and of the empty text, ` ` and `-` is `None`. `an object's angle is its dial reading, or its R1`: `sampleA` holding `QZd` put in by `withItem` at R1 30° turns at −20° (its reading, step 258), holding `QZ` at R1 45° at 45°, and holding nothing at R1 15° at 15°, each within 1e-12. `NamingTemplateTests`' facts pass unchanged. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the slot bar's pure halves land, `PickLetter` MUST exist in `Setups.fs`, `SetupSlot.fittingItems` MUST list the items whose model fits the slot, `pickedByLetter` MUST pick the next fitting item whose label starts with the typed letter and never the slot's own, and `turnAngle` MUST be the one angle rule `NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf` calls; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot lists the kit's items that fit it, in their order`, `a typed letter picks the next fitting item whose label starts with it, wrapping, and never the slot's own` and `an object's angle is its dial reading, or its R1`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.
